# Task 2: California Housing Price Prediction Using Ridge and Lasso Regression

## Datheon Machine Learning & Data Science Internship

### Project Overview

This project focuses on predicting median house values using the California Housing dataset. It implements and compares Ordinary Least Squares (OLS), Ridge Regression (L2 regularization), and Lasso Regression (L1 regularization) to evaluate their predictive performance and understand the impact of regularization on linear regression models.

### Objectives

- Predict median house values using regression techniques.
- Perform exploratory data analysis (EDA) and visualize feature correlations.
- Handle missing values through appropriate imputation techniques.
- Engineer interaction features to capture relationships between variables.
- Analyze multicollinearity among input features.
- Standardize continuous features and encode categorical attributes where applicable.
- Tune Ridge and Lasso regularization parameters using GridSearchCV.
- Compare model performance using RMSE, MAE, and R².

### Dataset

- **Dataset:** California Housing
- **Target Variable:** `median_house_value`
- **Source:** [California Housing Dataset (CSV)](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ageron/handson-ml2/master/datasets/housing/housing.csv)

The dataset contains housing-related information, including location, housing age, rooms, population, households, and median income.

### Technologies and Libraries

- Python
- Pandas
